  "company": "TripActions",
  "role": "Director of Design",
  "summary": "Onboarding, sign-in, and navigation work that created clearer connections between TripActions travel and expense products.",
  "overview": "I redesigned onboarding, sign-in, and initial product flows for member and non-member customers. In a separate Liquid tiger team, I worked with product design, product management, growth marketing, and engineering to explore a more unified experience across travel and expense.",
  "projectBrief": {
    "context": "TripActions was expanding from corporate travel into expense management, creating new onboarding and navigation needs across related products.",
    "challenge": "Member and non-member customers needed clearer entry flows, while administrators had no visibility into the new expense product after signing in.",
    "contribution": "I redesigned core onboarding, sign-in, and initial screens. In a separate Liquid tiger team, I led visual and UX exploration, proposed unified directions and alternate navigation flows, and delivered Figma screen designs to product leadership.",
    "approach": "I worked across product design, product management, growth marketing, engineering, and web to connect travel and expense through a more consistent visual and navigation language.",
    "outcome": "The proposed experience resolved the product-discovery gap. Parts of the work were adopted at launch, and the broader visual direction informed the later TripActions-to-Navan transition."
  },
